# Deploy local and prod

When the user asks to deploy (local, prod, or both), a **local agent** on the Windows repo (`D:\sf\OnPointCall`) should run the scripts below. Do not invent `migrate:fresh`, `docker compose down -v`, or other wipes.

Cloud agents cannot reach Windows Docker or the VPS. Tell the user to run deploy from a local agent, or run the scripts themselves.

## Commands (repo root)

PowerShell (Windows local agent):

```powershell
powershell -File scripts/deploy.ps1 both
powershell -File scripts/deploy.ps1 local
powershell -File scripts/deploy.ps1 prod
```

Git Bash / WSL:

```bash
bash scripts/deploy.sh both
bash scripts/deploy.sh local
bash scripts/deploy.sh prod
```

## What they do

- **local:** `git checkout master` + `git pull origin master`, then `php artisan migrate --force` and cache clear in Docker. Aborts if the working tree is dirty.
- **prod:** SSH to host alias `onpoint-prod` (or `ONPOINT_PROD_SSH`), `git reset --hard origin/master` in `/opt/onpointcall`, then migrate + cache + restart. Forward-migrate only.

## Prerequisites

- Changes must already be on GitHub `master` (PR merged).
- Docker Desktop running for local.
- One-time SSH config for prod (`Host onpoint-prod` in `~/.ssh/config`). If SSH fails, print the config snippet from `scripts/deploy-prod.sh` and stop.

## After deploy

- Local: http://localhost/admin
- Prod: health check is part of `scripts/prod-update.sh` (`curl http://localhost/up` on the VPS)
